hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"10891","I am Muhammad bin Muammar, we are Al-Mughirah bin Salamah Abu Hisham Al-Makhzoumi, we are Abdul-Wahid bin Ziyad, we are Othman bin Hakim, we are Abdul Al-Rahman bin Shaybah said: I heard Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: I said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: What do we have to do? Are we mentioned in the Qur’an as men are mentioned? She said: One day at noon, I was not disturbed by his call from the pulpit. She said: While I was combing my head, I wrapped my hair, then I went out to The room of my house, so I put my ear to the ground, and behold, he was saying from the pulpit: “O people, God says in His Book: Muslim men and women, until the end of the verse: God has prepared for them forgiveness and a great reward.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10892","I am Al-Qasim bin Zakaria, Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Aqmar, on the authority of Al-Aghar, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, and my father Hurairah, they said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever wakes up during the night and wakes up his wife and prays two rak’ahs together, they are prescribed Theirs is a night of remembering God often, both men and women.”"
"10893","I am Muhammad bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Hammad bin Zaid, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, who said: Zaid came to complain about his wife to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he commanded him to hold it, and God Almighty revealed: “And hide within yourself that which God will reveal.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10894","I am Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna. He said: Abdul Wahhab told me, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Masruq, that Aisha said: O Abu Aisha “Three, whoever says one of them has committed the greatest libel against God.” He said: And I was reclining and sat up, so I said: O Mother of the Believers, Wait for me and do not rush me. Did you see the words of God Almighty: And He saw it on the clear horizon, and He saw it at another coming. She said: “It is only He is Gabriel, peace be upon him. He saw him once as he was created and in the image in which he was created, and he saw him another time when he descended from the sky to the earth, masterless. The greatness of His creation is between the heaven and the earth.” She said: “I was the first to ask the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about this verse. He said: “He is Gabriel, “And whoever claims that he knows what will happen tomorrow has committed a grave lie against God, and God says: Say, ‘Whoever is in the heavens does not know. And the earth is unseen except Allah, and they do not know when they will be resurrected. And whoever claims that Muhammad concealed something of what Allah revealed to him, then he has done more to Allah than to Him. Lies, and God says: O Messenger, convey what has been sent down to you from your Lord, and if you do not do so, then you have not conveyed His message, and God will protect you. Of the people. Indeed, God does not guide the disbelieving people. She said: If Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, had concealed anything of what was revealed to him, he would have concealed this verse: And when you said to the one upon whom God had bestowed, and upon whom you had bestowed, “Keep your wife to yourself, and fear God,” and you concealed within yourself what God will reveal, and you feared people, and God is more worthy that you should fear Him.” I am Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna, on the authority of Ibn Abi Adi, and Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Masruq On the authority of Aisha, something similar, and he said: Yazid told us, he said: Dawud told us, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, he said: I was with Aisha, so he mentioned Towards him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10895","I am Suwayd bin Nasr, I am Abdullah, I am Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, who said: When Zainab’s waiting period had passed, the Messenger of God said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, to Zaid: “Recite it to me.” Zaid said: So I set off and said: O Zainab, give good news. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent And he greeted you, mentioning you, and she said: I will not do anything unless I command my Lord. So she got up to her mosque, and the Qur’an was revealed, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came. May God bless him and grant him peace, until he entered upon her without permission.”"
"10896","I am Ishaq bin Ibrahim, I am Al-Mala’i, this is Isa bin Tahman. He said: I heard Anas say: Zainab used to boast about the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him: God Almighty granted me marriage from heaven, and in it the verse about the veil was revealed. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, left while they were sitting, then he returned. While they were sitting in the house, until this was seen on his face, then God Almighty revealed: O you who have believed, do not enter the houses of the Prophet unless You will be given permission to eat food, not knowing where it is.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10897","I am Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid, narrated by Sufyan, narrated by Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, who said: I am among the people, when a woman said: I have given myself to you, O Messenger of God, so consider your opinion, O Messenger of God. Then a man stood up and said: Marry her to me. He said: “Go.” So ask for even an iron ring.” Then he went and did not bring anything, not even an iron ring. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You have with you some “Are there any surahs of the Qur’an?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “So he married it to whatever surahs of the Qur’an he had with him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10898","I am Amr bin Ali, we are Marhum Al-Attar, we are Thabit, on the authority of Anas, that a woman came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, exposing herself, and he said: I have no need for women.” A daughter said to Anas: “What was her most beautiful face?” Anas said: “She was better than you. She desired the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” May God bless him and grant him peace, so she offered herself to him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10899","It is narrated by Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Abu Usama, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “I was I am jealous of those who sacrificed themselves to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I say: Should a woman sacrifice herself? Then God Almighty revealed: Hope whomever you wish of them, and you may take to yourself whomever you wish.” I said: “By God, I do not see your Lord but hastening for you in your desires.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10900","I am Muhammad bin Abdullah, I am Abu Hisham, narrated by Wahib, he said: narrated by Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of Aisha, She said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not die until God made it lawful for him to marry as many women as he wanted.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10901","I am Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala, narrated by Muhammad bin Thawr, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Anas, who said: When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, got married And he greeted Zainab. Umm Sulaim gave him a living in a stone basket. Anas said: He said to me: “Go and invite whoever of the Muslims you meet,” so I called. He had whomever I met, so they began to enter and eat and leave, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, put his hand in the food, put it into it, and said, “What?” God willing, he would say, “I did not leave anyone I met without inviting him.” They ate until they were satisfied, and they left, and a group of them remained, so they lingered over him. Hadith, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, became ashamed to say anything to them, so he went out and left them at home, so God Almighty revealed: O you who have believed, do not enter the houses of the Prophet unless permission is given to you to eat food, without looking at it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10902","Muhammad ibn Hatim ibn Nu`aym informed us, he said: Suwayd informed us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Bayan ibn Bishr, he said : I heard Anas bin Malik say in this verse: “O you who have believed, do not enter the houses of the Prophet unless permission is given to you to eat.” He said: Built. The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, accompanied some of his wives, and they prepared food, so they sent and called men and they ate, then he got up and went out, and came to the house of Aisha and I followed him. He entered and found two men in her house. When he saw them, he returned and did not speak to them. They got up and went out, and the verse about the Hijab was revealed: “O you who have believed, do not enter the houses of the Prophet unless you have been given permission.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10903","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Humaid told us, that Anas said: Omar, may God be pleased with him, said, I said: “Oh Messenger of God, both the righteous and the ungodly will come upon you, but if you veil the mothers of the believers, then God Almighty has revealed the verse of veiling.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10904","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Ibn Abi Omar told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “I was eating with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, living in Qaab, when Omar, may God be pleased with him, passed by, so he invited him and he ate. Then his finger touched my finger, and he said: He felt, or oh, if he had obeyed, it would be as no eye has seen. So the veil descended. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10905","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir told us, on the authority of his father, he said: Abu Majliz told us, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, He said: “When the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, married Zainab bint Jahsh, he called the people and they ate, then they sat down and talked. He said: Then it seemed as if He was preparing to stand up, but they did not stand up. When he saw that, one of the people who stood up stood up, and three sat down. He said: And the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came. To enter, then the people were sitting, then they got up and left, so I came and informed the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that they had set off. Then he came until he entered. He said: So I went to enter, and he threw the veil between me and him, may God bless him and grant him peace, and God Almighty revealed: O Those who have believed, do not enter the houses of the Prophet unless you are given permission to eat food without looking at its content. But when you are invited, then enter, and when you are fed, disperse. Indeed, this was great in the sight of God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10906","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abu Qutaybah told us, he said: Issa bin Tahman told us, he said: I heard Anas bin Malik, saying: “ And when you ask them for anything, ask them from behind a veil. He said: It was revealed about Zainab bint Jahsh."
"10907","Ali bin Hajar told us, on the authority of Ismail, he said: Abdullah bin Dinar told us, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “My likeness and the likeness of the prophets is like a man who built a building and improved it and made it beautiful, except for the place of a brick. One of his corners, so he made the people go around it, admire him, and say to him: Could you please place this brick, for I am where the brick was. “And I am the Seal of the Prophets.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10908","Muhammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ibn al-Qasim told us, on the authority of Malik, he said: Na’im al-Mujmar told me that Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Zaid told him, on the authority of Abu Masoud Al-Ansari, that he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us in the presence of Saad bin Ubadah. Bashir bin Saad said to him: God commanded us to pray for you, so how can we pray for you? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was silent until we wished he had not asked him, then he said: “Say: O God, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You have blessed the family of Abraham, and you have blessed Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, just as you have blessed the family of Abraham. In the worlds, you are Praiseworthy and Glorious, and peace, as you have \"You knew\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10909","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: A spirit told us, he said: Awf told us, on the authority of Khalas, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Moses, peace be upon him, was alive and concealed, not showing anything of his skin out of shyness. Then some of the Children of Israel harmed him, and they said: What He covered himself with this veil except for something on his skin, either leprosy, or a boil, or a disease. So he went in to wash himself, and put his clothes on the stone, and they returned. The stone was covered with his clothes, and he went out, continuing his pursuit, and the children of Israel saw that he was the best-mannered of people, and he was clear of what they were saying. That was his saying. God Almighty: O you who have believed, do not be like those who annoyed Moses. Ishaq ibn Ibrahim told us, he said: Al-Nadr informed us, on the authority of Awf. With this chain of transmission, the same as it"
"10910","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Omar bin Hafs bin Ghayath told me, he said: my father told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, he said: he told me Amr ibn Murrah, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: When it was revealed: “And warn your closest kindred, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went up May God bless him and grant him peace, and he began to call out: “O Banu Fihr, O Banu Adiy, O Banu so-and-so,” to the clans of Quraysh, until they gathered together, and the man made If he was not able to get out, he sent a messenger to see, and Abu Lahab came and the Quraysh gathered together, and he said: “What if I told you that Horses in the valley wanting to attack you. Did you believe me? They said: Yes, we have only tried to tell the truth about you. He said: “For I am a warner to you before a severe torment.” Abu Lahab said: May you be cursed, everyone. Today, is this why you gathered us together and it was revealed: Abu Lahab’s hands have dried up?"
"10911","Abdah bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of Suwayd, on the authority of Zuhair, he said: Asim told us, on the authority of Abu Uthman, he said: Abu Musa told me, He said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey, and the people overlooked a valley, so they loudly shouted “Allahu Akbar” and “Allah is Great” and “God is great, God is great.” Akbar, there is no god but Allah, and Asim raised his voice, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O people, be content with yourselves. Indeed, the one who “Whatever you call upon is not deaf, for He is Hearing and Near, for He is with you.” He repeated it three times. Abu Musa said: He heard me say while I was behind him: There is neither power nor power. There is no power except in God. He said: “O Abdullah bin Qais, shall I not direct you to a word from the treasures of Paradise?” I said: Yes, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you. He said: “There is no power nor strength except in God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10912","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Muammar, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Masoud, He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the mosque and around the Kaaba were sixty and three hundred monuments, so he began stabbing them with a stick in his hand, and made He says: “The truth has come and falsehood has vanished. Verily, falsehood has vanished and: The truth has come. And who initiates falsehood and does not restore it?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10913","Ahmad bin Yahya bin Al-Wazir bin Sulayman told us, saying: I heard Ibn Wahb saying: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Anas bin Malik said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever is pleased to have his provision extended to him, or for his sake to be forgotten, May he maintain his ties of kinship.”"
"10914","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Dhar, he said: I was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the mosque at sunset, and he said: “Do you know where the sun sets?” I said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: “It will go until it ends under the Throne with its Lord, then it will ask for permission and permission will be given to it, and it is about to come.” She asks for permission, but it is not given to her. She intercedes and asks, and when that is said, it is said: Get out of your place, for that is the saying of God Almighty: And the sun runs to its resting place.”"
"10915","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Shibl told us, he said: I heard Abu Qaza’ah, speaking Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Hakim bin Muawiyah, on the authority of his father, that he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Muhammad, I swore By the number of my fingers, I will not follow you, nor follow your religion, so I ask you by God: What has God sent you with? He said: “Islam: bearing witness that there is no god but God, and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, establishing prayer, and paying zakat, brothers and sisters, it is not accepted. “May God repent from anyone who associates anything with God after his conversion to Islam.” He said: What is the right of the wife of one of us upon him? He said: “You feed her when you feed her, and you clothe her when you clothe her, and you do not strike her in the face, and you do not revile her, and you do not leave her except in the house.” He pointed with his hand to the Levant and said: “Here you will be gathered, riding and on foot, and on your faces on the Day of Resurrection. With your mouths, you will give birth to seventy nations. You are the last of them and the most honorable of them in the sight of God. And the first thing that is expressed on one of you is his thigh.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10916","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid, meaning Ibn Al-Harith, told us on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, he said: Al-Harith bin told me Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Salem bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to order us to reduce And he leads us to believe in the pure ones.”"
"10917","Al-Rabīʿ ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā informed us, saying: Ādam narrated to us, saying: Shaybān Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated to us, saying: Qatādah narrated to us, saying: I heard Anas ibn Mālik say: The Messenger of Allāh ﷺ said:\n\n\"Allāh will gather the believers on the Day of Resurrection, and they would say: 'If only we could seek intercession from our Lord so that He might give us relief from our place here.' They will set out until they come to Ādam, peace be upon him, and say: 'O Ādam, you are the father of mankind. Allāh created you with His own Hand, breathed into you of His Spirit, prostrated the angels before you, and taught you the names of all things. Intercede for us with your Lord so that He may give us relief from our place here.' He will say: 'I am not fit for that,' and he will mention his sin which he committed by eating from the tree. 'But go to Nūḥ, peace be upon him, for he is the first messenger Allāh sent.' They will come to Nūḥ, and he will say: 'I am not fit for that,' and he will mention his sin which he committed by asking his Lord that of which he had no knowledge. 'But go to Ibrāhīm, peace be upon him, the Khalīl of al-Raḥmān.' They will come to Ibrāhīm, and he will say: 'I am not fit for that,' and he will mention his three lies: his saying, 'Indeed, I am sick' (Q 37:89); his saying, 'Rather, this one, the greatest of them, did it' (Q 21:63); and his saying to Sārah when he came before the tyrant: 'Tell him that I am your brother, for I shall tell him that you are my sister, for we are siblings in the Book of Allāh, and there is no other believing man or woman on earth besides us.' 'But go to Mūsā, peace be upon him, the one to whom Allāh spoke and whom He gave the Tawrāh.' They will come to Mūsā, peace be upon him, and he will say: 'I am not fit for that,' and he will mention his sin which he committed by killing the man. 'But go to ʿĪsā, peace be upon him, the servant and messenger of Allāh, a Word from Allāh and a Spirit from Him.' They will come to ʿĪsā, and he will say: 'I am not fit for that. But go to Muḥammad ﷺ, a servant whose past and future sins Allāh has forgiven.'\"\n\nThe Messenger of Allāh ﷺ said: \"They will come to me, and I will seek permission from my Lord, and permission will be granted me to approach Him. When I see my Lord, I will fall in prostration, and He will leave me as long as He wills. Then He will say to me: 'Raise your head, O Muḥammad. Speak and you will be heard; intercede and your intercession will be accepted; ask and you will be given.' I will raise my head and praise my Lord with praises He teaches me. Then I will intercede, and He will set a limit for me, and I will bring them out of the Fire and admit them into Paradise. Then I will return to my Lord a second time and fall in prostrate, and He will say to me the like of that. I will raise my head, and He will set a limit for me, and I will bring them out of the Fire and admit them into Paradise. Then I will return to my Lord a third time and fall in prostrate for Him, and He will say to me the like of that. I will raise my head, and He will set a limit for me, and I will bring them out of the Fire. Then I will return a fourth time and say: 'O my Lord, there remains in the Fire only those whom the Qurʾān has confined.' He will say: 'Yes, and upon whom eternity has become binding.'\"\n\nQatādah said: \"And that is the Maqām Maḥmūd (the Praiseworthy Station).\""
"10918","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’, on the authority of Tamim Al-Tai, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out to us and said: “Don’t you line up as the angels line up before their Lord?” They said: Oh. Messenger of God, and how do the angels line up before their Lord? He said: “They complete the row in front, and stand in line in the row.”"
"10919","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He came to Khaybar, and we prayed there in the morning. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rode, and Abu Talha rode, and I was Abu Talha’s sergeant. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ran into an alley in Khaybar, and his thigh was exposed to the point that I could see the white of his thigh. So he came to Khaybar. So he said: “When we camped in a people’s place, the morning of those who had been warned became bad.” He said: And they went out to their work, so they said: Muhammad, Abdul said. Al-Aziz: Some of our companions said: And on Thursday, he said: So we hit her by force, he said: Then the captives gathered, and Dihya came, and he said: O Messenger of God Give me a slave girl from captivity. So he said: “Go and take a slave girl.” So he took Safiyya, and a man said: O Messenger of God, is he taking Safiyya? It is only suitable for you. So he said: “Call him.” So he came, and when he looked at her, he said: “Take another one.” So he freed her and married her. It was said: O Abu Hamza, how can I believe her? He said: She believed it herself (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10920","Ibrahim bin Muhammad told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Yahya bin Amara, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr. On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Abu Talib fell ill, so Quraysh came to him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to visit him and visit his head. A man’s seat, so Abu Jahl came and sat in it, then he said: Don’t you see that your nephew is falling in love with our gods? He said: My nephew, why do your people accuse you? He said: “I want them to accept a word for which the Arabs owe them, and the non-Arabs pay the tribute to them.” He said: What is it? He said: “There is no god but Allah.” So they said: Did He make the gods one god? So the verse “S” was revealed, and he recited until he reached: “Ijab.” Al-Hasan bin Ahmad bin Habib informed us, saying: Muhammad, who is the son of Abdullah bin Numayr, he said: Abu Usama told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, he said: Abbad told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, and the like. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10921","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told me, he said: Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Omar bin Dhar, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prostrated in: p. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10922","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ubaid. By God, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was praying, and Satan came to him, seized him, struck him, and strangled him. The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Until I found the cold of his tongue against my hand, and had it not been for the invitation of my brother Suleiman, peace be upon him, he would have been bound so that the people could see him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10923","Muhammad bin Bashar informed us, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: Shu`bah informed us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ziyad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “A demon from the jinn escaped yesterday to interrupt my prayers, so God enabled me to control him, so I captured him and wanted to I tie it to one of the poles of the mosque so that you can see it. So I remembered the invitation of my brother Suleiman bin Dawud, and his saying: My Lord, forgive me. He granted me a kingdom that no one after me should have, so I rejected him in disgrace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10924","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abd al-Aziz bin Abd al-Samad informed us, he said: Abu Imran al-Juniy told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdullah bin Qais, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What is between the people and them looking at Their Lord, except the veil of arrogance upon his face in the Gardens of Eden.”"
"10925","Amr bin Sawad bin Al-Aswad bin Amr told us, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Ata’, on the authority of Sa’id bin Yassar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The angels attend the dead, so when He was a righteous man. He said: Come out, O good soul. It was in a good body. Come out virtuous, and give good tidings of a good spirit and fragrance and a good Lord. Angry, they say that until it comes out, then it is taken up to heaven, and the opening is opened for it, and it is said: Who is this? It is said: So-and-so, then it is said: Welcome to the good soul, if it is in a good body, enter, virtuous, and bring good tidings of a spirit and fragrance and a God who is not angry, and that will be said to it. Until it reaches the seventh heaven, and when it is an evil man, it is said: Come out, O evil soul. It was in an evil body. Come out of Dhimimah, and give good tidings of hot and dark, and others similar to it in pairs, and that will be said until it comes out, then it will be taken up to heaven, Then it is opened for it, and it is said: Who is this? It is said: So-and-so, and it is said: No, the evil soul is welcome, it was in an evil body, come out. You are reprehensible, and the gates of heaven will not be opened to you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10926","Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi told us, he said: Mu`tamar, meaning Ibn Sulayman, told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Sulayman, on the authority of my father Saleh, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Adam and Moses protested, and he said: O Adam, you are the one whom God created with His hand. And He breathed His spirit into you, and you deceived people and expelled them from Paradise. Then Adam said: And you, Moses, whom God chose by His words, blame me for an act “What did I do? God wrote it down for me before He created the heavens and the earth.” He said: “So Adam performed Hajj to Moses.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10927","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr ibn Musawar informed us, saying: Hammad told us, on the authority of Marwan Abu Lubabah, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “ The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to fast until we told him what he wanted to break his fast, and he would break his fast until we told him what he wanted to fast, and he would recite in Every night the children of Israel and the marches.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10928","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahim told us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr bin Issa Al-Humaidi told us, he said: Sufyan told us, He said: Omar bin Saeed Al-Thawri told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, he said: I heard Saeed bin Jubayr, saying: No one is more patient with harm he hears from God. They will call upon Him as a rival to Him, and then He will provide for them and heal them.” Al-A’mash said: So I said to him: From whom did you hear it, O Abu Abdullah? He said: Abu Abdullah told us about it. Abdul Rahman Al-Salami, on the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10929","Hanad bin Al-Sirri told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “God, Blessed and Most High, says: Whoever I take away his two generous things, and he seeks reward and is patient, I have not given him a reward short of Paradise.”"
"10930","Muhammad bin Amir told us, he said: Mansur bin Salamah told us, he said: Ya’qub told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar said: “This verse was revealed, and we do not know about what it was revealed about: Then on the Day of Resurrection you will dispute before your Lord,” we said. “Who should we dispute with?” There was no dispute between us and the People of the Book, until strife broke out. \"in it\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10931","Muhammad bin Kamil informed us, he said: Hushaym informed us, on the authority of Husayn bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, on the authority of His father, he said: We went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we were on a journey one night. We said: O Messenger of God, if you would have intercourse with us? He said: “I am afraid that you will sleep, so who will wake us up for prayer?” Bilal said: I am, O Messenger of God. So the people got ready and they lay down, and Bilal supported him. To his mount, his eyes overwhelmed him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, woke up and the visor of the sun had risen. He said: “O Bilal, where is what you said?” He said: O Messenger of God, by the One who sent you with the truth, I have never been given a sleep like this. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God He took your souls when He wished, and restored them to you when He wished. Then he commanded them to spread out for their need, and they performed ablution as the sun had risen, so he prayed. They have the dawn (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10932","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ya’la told me, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: They killed people of polytheism, and they multiplied, then they came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Indeed, what you say and call to is good. If you had told us that for what we had done there would be an atonement, then it was revealed: “And those who call upon no other god with God and do not kill,” and it was revealed: “O My servants who \"They were extravagant over themselves.\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10933","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Jarir informed us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: A Jewish rabbi came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Abu al-Qasim, when the Day of Resurrection comes, God will place the heavens on A finger, and the two earths are on a finger, and the water and the earth are on a finger, and the trees are on a finger, and all the creatures are on a finger, then He shakes them. He says: I am the king. I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, laughing until his eyes showed astonishment at what he said, and out of belief in him. Then he recited: “And they have not estimated God as He deserves, while the earth as a whole will take it on the Day of Resurrection.”"
"10934","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Mansour and Sulayman told me, on the authority of Ibrahim, On the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah: “A Jew came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Muhammad, God holds the heavens over A finger, and the two earths are on a finger, and the mountains and creatures are on a finger. He said: Then he says: I am the king. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, laughed. And he greeted, until his molars became visible, and he said: “And they have not esteemed God according to His esteem.” Yahya said: Fudayl ibn Iyad added to it, on the authority of Mansour, On the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ubaida, on the authority of Abdullah: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, laughed in astonishment and astonishment. Abu Abdul Rahman said : Issa bin Yunus disagreed with him, he narrated it on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10935","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Issa bin Yunus told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abd God, he said: “A man from the People of the Book came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: God Almighty holds the heavens on a finger. He carries the two lands on one finger, and He carries the water and the earth on one finger, and He carries the trees on one finger, and He carries all of creation on one finger. Then he said: I am the king. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, laughed until his molars became visible. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10936","Suwayd bin Nasr informed us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Anbasa bin Saeed, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Amra, on the authority of Mujahid, he said Ibn Abbas said: Aisha told me that she asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about his saying, the Almighty: “And the earth as a whole.” I will hold him on the Day of Resurrection while the heavens are folded with his right hand: Where will the people be on that day? He said: On the bridge of Hell."
"10937","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Abd al-Hamid bin Saleh Abu Saleh told us, he said: Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Al-A'mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “All the people of Paradise say: Were it not that God He guided me, and there will be thanks to him, and all the people of Hell will say: If God had guided me, it would be a regret for him.”"
"10938","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Sa`id bin told me Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, used to say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God will hold the two earths together on the Day of Resurrection, and fold The heavens with his right hand, then he says: I am the king, where are the kings of the earth?"
"10939","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Suleiman. H, and Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, saying: Ibn Abi Adiy told us, on the authority of Sulayman al-Taymi, on the authority of Aslam, on the authority of Bishr ibn Shaghaf, On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: A Bedouin asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: What are pictures? Suwayd said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: What are the pictures? He said: “A horn that is blown into.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10940","Muhammad bin Abdul Rahim told us, on the authority of Yunus bin Muhammad, he said: Abraham told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, and Abdul Rahman Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not give me a choice over Moses, for the people will be shocked on the Day of Resurrection, so I will be He is the first to wake up. Then, behold, Moses was rushing beside the throne. I do not know whether he was struck and woke up before me, or was he among those whom God excluded? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10941","Musa told us, he said: Al-Hasan bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Shababah, he said: Abdul Aziz told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Fadl, On the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Do not differentiate between the prophets of God, for the trumpet is blown and it is stunned.” Who is in the heavens and who is on earth except whom God wills? Then it will be blown again, and I will be the first to be sent. Then, Moses, peace be upon him, was taking By the Throne, I do not know whether I will be held accountable for his shock on the Day of Mount, or whether he was resurrected before me, and I do not say: “No one is better than Yunus ibn Matthew.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10942","Ahmad ibn Harb told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “There are forty days between the two blasts.” They said: O Abu Hurairah, forty days? He said: I refused. They said: Forty months? He said: I did not. They said: Forty years? He said: I refuse. He said: “Then God, Blessed and Most High, sends down water from the sky, and they sprout as plants sprout.” He said: “And nothing of mankind.” Only one bone will decay, and that is the tailbone.” He said: “And in it creation will be assembled on the Day of Resurrection.”"
"10943","Muhammad bin Hatim told us, he said: Hibban told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Aflah bin Saeed, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Rafi’ mentions that Umm Salamah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, one day on the pulpit, and he said: “O People,” she said, while she was combing her head, then she turned her head and got up from behind her room, and heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: O people, “While I was at the Basin, groups passed by you, taking you on the roads, so I called to you: ‘Come to the road.’ Then a caller would call out from Behind me: They changed it after you, so I say: Shatter it, shame it! (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10944","Muhammad bin Shuja’ told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj bin Abi Uthman, he said: Abu Al-Zubayr told me, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Al-Zubair, speaking on this pulpit, said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say the salutation: “There is no god but God, alone, with no partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him is praise, and He is capable of all things. There is no power nor strength except in God, there is no god but God, no We worship none but Him, the people of grace, grace, and good praise, there is no god but God, sincere in religion to Him, even if the disbelievers hate it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10945","Hanad bin Al-Sari told us, on the authority of Abda, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Asi, that he was asked: What is the worst thing you have seen? Did the Quraysh reach the level of knowledge from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: He passed by them one day, and they said to him: Are you the one who forbids us to worship what our fathers worshiped? He said: “I,” so they stood up to him and took him by the bundle of his clothes. He said: I saw Abu Bakr hugging him from behind him, screaming, and his eyes They laughed, and he said: Will you kill a man when he says, “My Lord is God?”"
"10946","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “But If one of you dies, his seat will be presented to him in the morning and evening. If he is one of the people of Paradise, then he is from the people of Paradise, and if he is one of the people of Hell. He will be among the people of Hell, until God resurrects him on the Day of Resurrection.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10947","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Dhar. H And Hanad bin Al-Sari informed us, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Dhar, on the authority of Yasa’, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Peace and blessings of God be upon him, in the words of God Almighty: “And your Lord says, ‘Call upon Me, I will respond to you.’ He said: Supplication is worship. Then he recited: Call upon Me. “I will respond to you. Indeed, those who are too disdainful to worship Me will enter Hell humiliated.” The wording is by Hannad. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10948","Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Hilal bin Osama, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Hakam, he said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O Messenger of God, a maid of mine was taking care of sheep for me, so I came to her and lost a sheep from the sheep. So I asked her about it, and she said: The wolf ate her, so I felt sorry for her, and I was one of the children of Adam, so I slapped her face while I was on my neck. Should I free her? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: “Where is God?” She said: In the sky. He said: “So who am I?” She said: You are the Messenger of God. He said: “ So free her.”"
"10949","Suleiman bin Dawud told us, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Ibn Jurayj told me that Abu al-Zubayr told him that Ali al-Asadi He told him that Abdullah bin Omar informed him that when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mounted his camel, he was going out on a journey. He said “Allahu Akbar” three times, and said: “Glory be to Him who has subjected this to us, and we would not have been near to it. {13} And indeed, to our Lord we are returning. {14}, O God, indeed we are We ask you on this journey of ours to do righteousness and piety, and of deeds that please you. O God, make this journey easy for us, and extend its distance from us. You are the companion in travel, and the successor in family. O God, I seek refuge in You from the hardships of travel, the gloom of the outlook, and the bad times in life. \"family and money\""
"10950","Abu Salih Al-Makki told us, he said: Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Masoud bin Malik, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I was victorious with youth, and Aad was destroyed with the hornet.”"
"10951","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Mansour told me, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Muammar. On the authority of Abdullah. H, and Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Muammar, on the authority of Abdullah, he said “A Thaqafiyan and a Qurayshi gathered at the house, and some of them said: Do you think God knows what we say? Some of them said: If we conceal, He will not know. And when we declared knowledge aloud, then God revealed: “And you did not conceal it, lest he bear witness against you.” And the wording is by Ibn Mansour. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10952","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Bahz bin Hakim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the Almighty’s saying: “Your hearing, and your sight, and your skins bear witness against you.” He said: “Indeed, you will be called.” And the first thing that appears on one of you is his thigh and his palm.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10953","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abu Qutaybah told us, he said: Suhail bin Abi Hazm told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited: “Indeed, those who said, ‘Our Lord is God,’ and then remained steadfast. He said, ‘The people said it, then they disbelieved, so whoever dies in it. He is one of the people of integrity.”"
"10954","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Bakra, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Indeed, the sun and the moon are two signs of God. They are not eclipsed by the death or life of anyone, but God frightens His servants through them,” said Abu Abd al-Rahman: Qatada disagreed with him."
"10955","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The sun and the moon do not eclipse due to the death or life of anyone, but they were created from His creation, God creates whatever He wills in His creation.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10956","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Bakr and Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Abu Qabil, on the authority of Shafi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out to us and said: “This is a book written by the Lord of the Worlds. In it are the names of the people of Paradise and the names of Their fathers, then the last of them will be summed up, so nothing will be added to them nor will anything be taken away from them. This is a book written by the Lord of the Worlds, in which are the names of the people of Hell. And naming their fathers, then he treated the last of them with kindness, so nothing could be added to or taken away from them.” They said: “So what is the work to do, O Messenger of God?” He said: “The worker of the people of Paradise will be sealed with the deeds of Paradise, even if he does any deed, and the one who works the Hellfire will be sealed with the deeds of Hell, even if he does any deed.” A work, God has finished creating it. He said: A party in Paradise and a party in the Hellfire."
"10957","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Maysara, he said: I heard Tawus saying: Ibn Abbas was asked about this verse: “Say: I do not ask you for any reward for it except affection for my kin,” Sa’id bin Jubayr: a relative of the family of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. Quraysh, and he was not related to them, so he said: “Unless you maintain the relationship between me and them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10958","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Saad told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God is more happy with the repentance of His servant than one of you who has lost his camel in the land of \"Deathly, he fears that hunger will kill him.\""
"10959","Abdah bin Abdullah told us, he said: Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Zakaria told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Salamah, on the authority of Al-Bahi On the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, he said: Aisha said: I did not know until Zainab entered upon me without permission while I was angry, then she said to the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace: It is sufficient for you, if Abu Bakr’s daughter turns two of her offspring for you, then comes to me, and I turn away from her, until The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Be victorious.” So I approached her and saw that her saliva had dried up in her mouth, and she did not respond to me at all. I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, his face shining. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10960","Ahmad bin Uthman bin Hakim told us, he said: Khalid bin Mukhlid told us, he said: Saeed bin Al-Sa’ib told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Yazid. Al-Ta'ifi, he said: We asked Ibn Abbas, we said: Who are these two men about whom the polytheists said what they said when they vented against the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? Peace and blessings of God be upon him, what has God given to people? He said: “As for the people of this town of Taif, Al-Mukhtar’s grandfather is Masoud bin Amr. As for the people of Mecca, he is a great man from The mighty men of Quraysh, and he did not name him for us.”"
"10961","Ali bin Hajar informed us, Ali bin Mushar said, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Thumama bin Uqba, on the authority of Zayd bin Arqam, he said: A man came from The Jews went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Do you claim that the people of Paradise eat and drink? He said: “By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, a man from among them will be given the strength of a hundred men in eating, drinking, intercourse, and desire.” So he said Man: Whoever eats and drinks will have a need, and there will be no harm in Paradise? Then he, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: “The need of one of them is a cold that comes out of his skin, and then his stomach becomes atrophied.”"
"10962","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, saying: Sufyan told us. H And Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Safwan bin Ya’la, on the authority of his father, He said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, reciting from the pulpit: “And call, O Malik.” And Ishaq said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace . . . (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10963","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Hujain bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abd al-Aziz bin Abi Salamah told us, on the authority of Ibn al-Fadl, On the authority of Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You saw me in Al-Hijr and the Quraysh.” You ask me about my secrets, so they asked me about things from the Holy House that I did not confirm, and I was in distress the likes of which I had never experienced before, so he raised it. God is mine to look to, and they never asked me about anything but I brought it to them, and you saw me in a group of prophets, and behold Moses, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he stood and prayed, and behold, there was a man with a wrinkled hair, as if he were one of the men of bad temper, and behold, Jesus was standing and praying, and the person closest to him looked like he was curled up. Ibn Masoud Al-Thaqafi, and behold, Ibrahim was standing, praying, and the people most like him were your companion, meaning himself, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the time had come for prayer. So I led them in prayer, and when I finished praying, someone said to me: O Muhammad, this is the owner of the Fire, so greet him, so he turned to me and began to greet me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10964","Muhammad bin Al-Ala told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, Abdullah said, “Indeed, the Quraysh It eluded the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He prayed for them to have years like the years of Joseph. They were afflicted with drought and fatigue until they ate bones. And he, meaning the man, began to look at the sky, and he saw between him and it an appearance of smoke from the effort, so God Almighty revealed: The day you come The sky with clear smoke {10} The people will be enveloped. This is a painful punishment {11} Then the Messenger of God was brought, and it was said: O Messenger of God, ask God for rain for them. For they had perished. So God asked for water, and they were given water. Then God Almighty revealed: Indeed, we will remove the torment for a little while. Indeed, you will return. So they returned to their state. which they were in when they were afflicted with prosperity, so God Almighty revealed: The day when we will strike with great force. Indeed, we will take revenge. He said: the day \"Badr\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10965","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, meaning Ibn al-Harith, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Furat al-Qazzaz told us On the authority of Abu al-Tufayl, on the authority of Hudhayfah ibn Usayd, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, informed us while we were remembering the hour, and he said: “The The Hour will not come until ten: the smoke, the antichrist, the rising of the sun from the west, the animal, and three eclipses: an eclipse in the east, An eclipse in the West, an eclipse in the Arabian Peninsula, the descent of Jesus, son of Mary, the conquest of Gog and Magog, and fire coming out of The bottom of Eden takes people to the gathering place.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10966","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Al-Nadr bin Shumail told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Mansour, and Sulayman, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, On the authority of Masruq, that Abdullah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when the Quraysh became difficult for him, said: “Oh God, help me with seven Like the seventh of Joseph.” Then one year took them and examined everything, and they ate the skins and the dead bodies. The other said: The skins and the bones, so he made to come out of The earth looked like smoke, so Abu Sufyan came and said: Your people have perished, so pray to God for them. He said: “If you return, we will return.” That is His statement: “The day the sky brings forth clear smoke {10} the people will be enveloped. This is a painful punishment {11}.” Abdullah said: Will the punishment of the Hereafter be revealed? Then Abdullah said: The smoke has passed."
"10967","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Abu Numan told us, he said: Thabit told us, he said: Hilal told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas “Abu Jahl said: Does Muhammad frighten us with the Zaqqum tree? Bring dates and butter and they will suffocate.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10968","Ismail bin Yaqoub told us, he said: Ibn Musa told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Ja`far, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, in this verse: “Have you seen someone who took his own desires as his god?” He said: “One of them was worshiping stones, so when he saw He is better than him. He threw it and worshiped the other.”"
"10969","Wahb bin Bayan told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Abu Salamah told me, he said Abu Hurairah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “God, Blessed and Most High, said: The son of Adam curses eternity, and I curse eternity. In my hand is the night and the day.”"
"10970","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Do not curse eternity, for God is eternity. God Almighty said: The son of Adam harms me. He curses eternity, while I am eternity, with my hand. Goodness, I turn night and day.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10971","Issa bin Hammad informed us, he said: Al-Layth bin Saad informed us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Saad, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yazid, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The people said: O Messenger of God, will we see our Lord on the Day of Resurrection? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do you have any trouble seeing the sun when there are no clouds below it, and do you have any trouble seeing the moon on the night?” “The full moon?” They said: “No.” He said: “And in this way you will see Him, the Almighty.” He said: “God will gather the people on the Day of Resurrection, and He will say: Whoever worships anything.” Let him follow him, for he who worships the sun will follow the sun, and he who worships the moon will follow the moon, and he who worships tyrants will follow tyrants, and you will remain This nation is full of its hypocrites, so God, Blessed and Most High, will come to them in the form that they recognize, and He will say: I am your Lord, and they will say: You are our Lord. So they will follow him, and the path will be struck between the two backs of Hell, so I and my nation will be the first to pass it, and only the messengers speak, and the call of the messengers On that day: O God, grant us peace, and in Hell there will be thorns like the thorns of lions. Have you seen the lions, for they are like the thorns of lions, except that they are not? No one knows the extent of its greatness except God Almighty, so it snatches people by their deeds, so if God Almighty wants to bring them out of the Fire by His mercy Whoever He wills, He commands the angels to bring out whoever does not associate anything with God, who says: There is no god but God, whoever God, Blessed and Most High, wills. That He would have mercy on him, so they would introduce them to Hell by the marks of prostration, and they would bring them out by the marks of prostration. God, Blessed and Most High, forbade Hell to the son of Adam. To eat away the traces of prostration, and they will be brought out of the fire while they have been engulfed, and the water of life will be poured upon them, and they will sprout as the seed sprouts in \"carrying the torrent\""
"10972","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Bishr, meaning Ibn al-Mufaddal, told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ya’la bin Ata, on the authority of Sufyan bin Abdullah Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of his father, said: I said: O Messenger of God, direct me to a matter in Islam that I will not ask anyone about after you. He said: “Say: I believe in God, then be upright.” He said: So what should I fear? He pointed to his tongue. “Muhammad bin Bashar told us, saying: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ya’la bin Ata, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sufyan Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of his father, similar to him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10973","Ali bin Al-Hussein told us, he said: Umayyah bin Khaled told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ziyad, he said: When he pledged allegiance to Muawiyah To his son, Marwan said: The Sunnah of Abu Bakr and Omar, and Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Bakr said: The Sunnah of Heraclius and Caesar, so Marwan said: This Concerning which God revealed: And he who said to his parents, “Is it for you?” This verse reached Aisha, and she said: He lied, by God, what is wrong with him? If I wanted to name what was revealed about it, I would name it, but the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed Marwan, and Marwan was in his loins. Marwan is a part of the curse of God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10974","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Ayyub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Hafs bin Ghayath told us, he said: Ibn Juraij told us, on the authority of Ata’, On the authority of Aisha, she said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a wind, he would stand up, sit down, come forward, and turn away. She said: So I told him Then he said: O Aisha, I do not believe that it will be as some people said: When they saw it crossing in the direction of their valleys, they said, “This is a random thing.” Our rain, rather, it is that which you hastened, a wind in which is a painful punishment.” He said: Then he sees drops, and he becomes calm, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10975","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sulayman bin Al-Mughirah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, he said: He told me Mahmoud bin Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Itban, so I met Itban, and he told me about him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No one bears witness.” There is no god but God, so fire will consume him, or fire will feed him.” Anas said: I liked this, so I said to my son: Write it down."
"10976","I am Suwayd bin Nasr, I am Abdullah, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, Mahmoud bin Al-Rabi’ told me, he said: I heard Itban bin Malik, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No servant will come in return on the Day of Resurrection saying: There is no god but God, seeking in that the face of God.” God Almighty has forbidden the Fire for him.”"
"10977","I am Muhammad bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Ibn Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he said: “I ask God for forgiveness a hundred times a day.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10978","I am Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi, narrated by Hammad, narrated by Asim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sargis, who said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He was sitting with some of his friends, so I turned behind him like this, and he knew what I wanted, so he threw the cloak off his back, and I saw the place of the ring on it. His shoulder sagged like a crowd, and around him were two horses, as if they were warts. So I came and met him, and said to him: May God forgive you, O Messenger of God. He said: “And to you.” Some of the people said: Did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ask forgiveness for you? He said: Yes, and for you, then he recited: And ask forgiveness for your sin and for the believing men and believing women."
"10979","I am Muhammad bin Hatim bin Nuaym, I am Hibban, I am Abdullah, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Abi Al-Mazard, he said: I heard my uncle Abu Al-Hubab Saeed bin Yasar He narrates, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Indeed, God Almighty created creation, so that when He had finished creating it, it would stand The womb, and she said: This is the place of the one who seeks refuge from severance. He said: Would you not be satisfied that I should uphold whoever has joined you, and sever whoever has severed you? She said: Yes, O My Lord, he said: It is yours.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “And recite, if you wish: Would it be possible for you, if you took charge, to cause corruption in the land and sever your ties of kinship {22} Those are those whom God has cursed and made deaf and blinded their sight {23} (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10980","I am Amr bin Ali, I am Yahya, I am Shu’bah, I am Qatada, on the authority of Anas, “Indeed, We have given you a clear victory.” He said: Al-Hudaybiyyah."
"10981","I am Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, narrated by Qarad, and he is Abdul-Rahman bin Ghazwan Abu Nuh, narrated by Malik, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Omar, said: We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey, and I asked him about something three times, but he did not answer me, so I said to myself: May your mother be bereaved of you, O Ibn Al-Khattab. So I mounted my mount and moved forward for fear that something had happened to me. Then I heard a caller calling: O Omar, So I came back thinking that something had been revealed about me, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Yesterday a surah was revealed to me that is more beloved to me than the world and all that is in it.” “Indeed, We have given you a clear victory {1} so that God may forgive you your previous sins and those that will follow.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10982","Narrated by Ali bin Hajar, narrated by Ismail, narrated by Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman, that Abu Yunus, the client of Aisha, told him, on the authority of Aisha, A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, asking him for a fatwa, while she was listening from behind the veil. He said: O Messenger of God, prayer overtakes me. While I am in a state of ritual impurity, should I fast? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “And prayer overtakes me while I am in a state of ritual impurity, so I fast.” He said: You are not like us, O Messenger of God. He has forgiven you. God will protect you from your past and future sins. He said: “By God, I hope to be the most fearful of you to God, and the most knowledgeable of you in what I fear.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10983","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, narrated by Abu Awanah, on the authority of Ziyad bin Alaqah, on the authority of Mughirah bin Shu’bah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed until His feet swelled, and it was said: Do you tolerate this, when God has forgiven you for your previous and future sins? He said: “Shall I not be a grateful servant?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10984","I am Amr bin Ali, and Abu Al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, who said: When this verse was revealed to the Prophet, he prayed May God bless him and grant him peace: Indeed, We have given you a clear conquest {1} so that God may forgive you for his return from Hudaybiyyah while they were mixed with sadness and depression. He slaughtered the sacrificial animal in Al-Hudaybiyyah, and said: “A verse has been revealed to me that is dearer to me than the whole world.” They said: O Messenger of God, we have learned. What does he do to you, what does he do to us? So it was revealed: “That He may admit the believing men and believing women into Gardens beneath which rivers flow,” as he said, “as a great victory.” The wording is by Amr. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10985","On the authority of Hilal bin Al-Ala’, on the authority of Hussein bin Ayyash, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Aazib, who said: A man used to recite in his house. Surah Al-Kahf, and next to him was a horse tied until a cloud covered it, and it began to approach and approach until the horse fled from it. He said The man: I was amazed at that. When the morning came, he came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and mentioned it to him and told it to him. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “ That tranquility was revealed for the Qur’an.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10986","I am Ahmad bin Sulaiman, we are Ya’la bin Ubaid, we are Abdul Aziz bin Siyah, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, he said: I came to Abu Wael I ask him about these people who Ali killed at Nahrawan, why they responded to him, why they separated from him, and why he made it lawful to kill them, and he said We were in Siffin, and when the killing began among the people of the Levant, Amr ibn al-Aas said to Muawiyah: Send Ali the Qur’an, and invite him to the Book of God. He will not refuse you, so a man brought him and said: Between us and you is the Book of God. Have you not seen those who are called to the Book of God to judge? among them, then a group of them turned away while they were turning away, and Ali, peace be upon him, said: I am more worthy of that, between us is the Book of God, so she came to him"
"10987","I am Ibrahim bin Saeed, on the authority of Shababah bin Suwar, on the authority of Abu Zubr Abdullah bin Al-Ala bin Zubr, on the authority of Busr bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Abi Idris, on the authority of Abi Ibn Ka’b, that he used to recite: 0 When those who disbelieved placed in their hearts the fever that was the fever of pre-Islamic times, even if you were protected as you were. They set out to ruin the Sacred Mosque. This reached Omar, and he was harsh to him, saying: You know that I used to go to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he would teach me what God had taught him. Omar said: Rather, you are a man who has knowledge and the Qur’an, so read and learn from what God and His Messenger have taught you."
"10988","I am Ali bin Al-Hussein, from Umayyah, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, and Husayn, on the authority of Salem bin Abi Al-Ja’d. He said: I asked Jabir bin Abdullah: “How many were you on the Day of the Tree?” He said: “One thousand and five hundred.”"
"10989","I am Muhammad bin Mansour, from Sufyan, on the authority of Amr, who said: I heard Jabir, saying: We were one thousand and four hundred on the day of Hudaybiyyah, so the Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Today you are the best people on earth.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10990","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, narrated by Al-Layth, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “No one will enter Hell.” He pledged allegiance under the tree.”"
"10991","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, narrated by Al-Layth, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, who said: “On the day of Hudaybiyyah, we were one thousand and four hundred. So we pledged our allegiance to him while Omar was holding him by the hand under the tree, which was a black tree. We pledged our pledge to him not to flee, but we did not pledge our allegiance to him to die.”"
"10992","On the authority of Ishaq bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Affan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, that some people from the people of Mecca descended on the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. peace be upon him from Mount Tanim at the dawn prayer, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took them and pardoned them, and God Almighty sent down “And it is He who withholds their hands from you and your hands from them,” the verse."
"10993","I am Muhammad bin Aqeel, I am Ali bin Al-Hussein, my father told me, on the authority of Thabit, he said: Abdullah bin Mughaffal Al-Muzani told me, he said: We were with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with Al-Hudaybiyyah at the root of the tree that God said, and it was as if I was a branch from the branches of that tree on The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, appeared, so I lifted him from his back, and Ali bin Abi Talib and Suhail bin Amr were in his hands, and he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Write: In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.” So Suhail took his hand and said: We do not know the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. Write. In our case, we do not know. He said: “Write in your name, O God. This is what Muhammad, the Messenger of God, reconciled with the people of Mecca,” so he held out his hand. He said: We have wronged you if you are a messenger. Write about our case what we know. He said: Write: This is what Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Muttalib, and I am the Messenger of God.” He said: So he wrote, “While we were like that, thirty young men armed with weapons came out against us, and they revolted in Our faces, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, called against them, so God took their sight, so we rose up to them and took them, and the Messenger of God said to them: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Have you come in the covenant of anyone, or has anyone made security for you?” So they said: No, so he cleared their way, and he descended. God Almighty: And it is He who withholds their hands from you, and your hands from them, until: the All-Seeing. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10994","I am Humayd bin Masada, from Bishr, meaning bin Al-Mufaddal, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wanted He requested that he write to the Romans, and they said: They do not read a book unless it is sealed, so he took a silver ring, as if I could see its whiteness. in his hand, and engraved on it: “Muhammad is the Messenger of God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10995","I am Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala, our Al-Mu`tamir is bin Sulaiman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: When it was revealed: O you who have believed, do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet, and do not speak loudly to him as some of you speak loudly to one another, lest you be discouraged. Your actions while you do not realize it. Thabit bin Qais said: By God, I am the one who used to raise my voice before the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And I fear that God has become angry with me. He said: So he became sad and turned sad, then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, lost him, so he asked about him, and said: O Prophet of God, he says: And I fear that I will be among the people of Hell, because I used to raise my voice before the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Rather, he is from the people of Paradise.” He said: We used to see him walking between us, a man from the people of Paradise. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10996","I am Al-Hasan bin Muhammad, from Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ibn Abi Mulaika told me that Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr told him that The caravan of Banu Tamim came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, said: Command Al-Qaqa’ bin Ma’abad, and Omar said: Rather. He ordered Al-Aqra' ibn Habis, and they continued until their voices rose, then it was said: O you who have believed, do not come forward before God. And His Messenger until the verse was completed: “And if they had been patient until it came out to them, it would have been better for them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10997","I am Muhammad bin Ali bin Al-Hasan bin Shaqiq. He said: My father told us. He said: I am Al-Hussein bin Waqid, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’: Those who call you from behind the rooms. He said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Indeed, my Hamdi is beautiful, and my Dhimmi are disgraceful, so he said: That is God, Blessed and Most High.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10998","Humayd ibn Masada, on the authority of Bishr, on the authority of Dawud, informed us on the authority of Amir. Abu Jubayrah ibn al-Dahhak said: “The verse was revealed about us.” The Messenger of God presented May God bless him and grant him peace in Medina, and there is not a man among us who does not have two or three names. Whenever he called a man by name, we would say: O Messenger of God, it is He becomes angry at this, so it was revealed: “And do not call one another by nicknames.” The entire verse."
"10999","I am Musa bin Saeed, we are Musaddad bin Mashad, we are Al-Mu`tamar bin Sulaiman, we are Abdul Razzaq, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Aamir bin Saad On the authority of his father, that Saad said: O Messenger of God, you gave so-and-so and so-and-so, and you prevented so-and-so while he was a believer. He said: “Muslim.” He said: You gave so-and-so He said it two or three times, all of which he said: “Muslim.”"
"11000","I am Ali bin Hajar, narrated by Ismail, narrated by Al-Ala, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do you know What is backbiting? They said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: He mentioned your brother in a way that he dislikes. It was said: What do you think if there is something in my brother that I would say? He said: “If what you say is true, then you have backbited him, and if it is not, then you have slandered him.”"
"11001","I am Saeed bin Yahya bin Saeed, from Ubayy, from Muhammad bin Qais, on the authority of Ataa bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas. Sa`id bin Yahya informed us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Muhammad bin Qais, on the authority of a man from Thaqif who is called Abu Awn, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “A delegation from Banu Asad came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they spoke and said: Mudar fought you, and we are not.” With the fewest of them in number, and not a thorn can eat them, we have reached your kinship. So he said to Abu Bakr and Omar, may God be pleased with them: “They spoke like this.” They said: No. He said: “The jurisprudence of these people is little, and Satan speaks on their tongues.” Ata’ said in his hadith: Then God Almighty revealed: “Yamnoun.” You must accept the verse (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11002","Imran bin Yazid told us, Ibn Abi Al-Rijal told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Umm Hisham bint Haritha bin Al-Numan, she said: “I never took the Qur’an and the Glorious Qur’an except from behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He used to lead the morning prayer with it.”"
"11003","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ziyad bin Ulaqah, he said: I heard my uncle, saying: I prayed with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited in one of the two rak’ahs: “By the palm trees in fields.” Shu’bah said: “I met him in the market in the crowd. He said: Q (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11004","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala informed us, saying: Muhammad, meaning Ibn Thawr, informed us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Heaven and Hell had a dispute, and Paradise said: O Lord, what is wrong with me that only the poor of people can enter me?” And their poor and fallen? And the fire said: O Lord, what is the matter with me that only the tyrannical and the arrogant enter upon me? So he said to the fire: You are my torment I may grant you whoever I wish, and he will say to Paradise: You are my mercy. I may grant you whoever I wish, and each one of you has its own fill. As for the people of Paradise, For God Almighty creates for it whatever He wills, and the people of Hell will be thrown into it, and you say: Is there anything more until he sets his foot in it? There They are filled and some of them flow into one another, and you say: “Quat, Qat, Qat.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11005","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amara, he is Ibn Ruwaybah, he said: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever prays before sunrise and before it sets will not enter Hell.” A man said to him: You heard him. Who is the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Yes, my ears heard it, and my heart understood it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"11006","Yahya bin Muhammad told us, he said: Yahya bin Kathir told us, he said: Abdullah bin Uthman told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, On the authority of Jarir, he said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he made us look at the moon on the night of the full moon, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He said: “As for you, you are looking at your Lord, Blessed and Most High, as you look at the moon, and you have no difficulty in seeing it. If you are able to Do not neglect two prayers: a prayer before the sunrise, and a prayer before its sunset, and recite: And glorify the praises of your Lord before the sunrise and before the sunrise. \"sunset\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11007","Muhammad bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Sallam bin Qutaybah, Hashim bin Al-Barid told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: “We were We pray behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the noon prayer, and we hear from him verse after verse from Surat Luqman, and Al-Dhariyat.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11008","Muhammad bin Al-Ala told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Masoud bin Malik, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I was victorious with youth, and Aad was destroyed with the hornet.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11009","Nasr bin Ali bin Nasr told us, he said: Abu Ahmad told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told me: “Indeed, I am the Sustainer, the Possessor of Power, the Firm.”"
"11010","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Zainab, the daughter of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, that she came to Mecca while she was sick, so she mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Tawaf behind praying while you were riding.” She said: I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, while he was at the Kaaba reciting the verse. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11011","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Al-Zuhri. H and Al-Harith bin Miskin. I read about it while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, who said: Malik told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Muhammad bin Jubayr bin Mutim, on the authority of his father, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, reciting the verse “At-Tur” in the Maghrib. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11012","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Thabit told us, on the authority of Anas: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned the House inhabited in the seventh heaven, and behold, Abraham, peace be upon him, was leaning his back against the House. Al-Ma’mur, and behold, seventy thousand angels entered it every day, and when they left it they would never return to it.”"
"11013","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, he said: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Ibn Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Masoud, in his saying: “The heart did not lie about what it saw. He said: He saw Gabriel, peace be upon him, in a garment of A vast expanse that has filled what is between the sky and the earth.”"
"11014","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yazid told us, meaning Ibn Zuray’, he said: Dawud told us, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, he said: I was with Aisha, and she said: O Abu Aisha, there are three people who speak about one of them has committed the greatest libel against God: “Whoever claims that Muhammad saw His Lord has certainly magnified the lie against God. He said: I was reclining and sat up, so I said: O Mother of the Believers, did not God say, “And He saw it on the horizon” Al-Mubin, and he saw it revealed another time, and she said: I was the first to ask about this verse, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Only.” That is Gabriel, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. I have never seen him in the form in which he was created except these two times. I saw him descending from the sky, motionless. The greatness of His creation is that which is between the heaven and the earth.” Then she said: Have you not listened to the words of God, Blessed and Most High: “Sights do not perceive Him while He perceives The All-Seeing, and He is the Gentle, the All-Aware. Have you not listened to the words of God: And it is not for a human being that God should speak to him except by revelation or from behind a veil. Or will He send a messenger and reveal by His permission whatever He pleases? And whoever claims that Muhammad concealed anything from the Book of God has committed the greatest libel against God, by God. He says: O Messenger, convey what has been sent down to you from your Lord, and whoever claims that he knows what will happen tomorrow has committed the greatest lie against God. And God says: Say, “No one in the heavens and earth knows the unseen except God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11015","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, in his saying: “I We have given you Al-Kawthar. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: It is a river in Paradise, its two rims are domes of pearls. So I said: O Gabriel. What is this? He said: It is Al-Kawthar, which God, Blessed and Most High, has given you, and the Sidra of the End has been raised for me, its end being in the seventh heaven. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11016","Ahmad bin Mani’ told us, he said: Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, he said: Al-Shaybani told us, he said: I asked Zirr bin Hubaysh about his saying: It was just around the corner, and he said: Ibn Masoud told me that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw Gabriel, peace be upon him, with six \"hundred wings\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11017","Al-Hussein bin Mansour told us, he said: Abdullah bin Numayr told us. H And Muhammad bin Al-Ala told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Husayn, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in his saying: “The heart did not lie about what it saw. It said: It saw it with its heart.” And Muhammad bin Al-Ala’ said: “The heart did not lie about what it saw.” He saw, he said: “He saw it twice in his heart.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11018","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Yazid bin Sharik, on the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: “ The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw his Lord, Blessed and Most High, with his heart, but he did not see Him with his sight. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11019","Yazid bin Sinan told me, he said: Yazid bin Abi Hakim told us, he said: Al-Hakam bin Aban told me, he said: I heard Ikrimah, saying: I heard Ibn Abbas say: “Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw his Lord, the Almighty and Majestic.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11020","Yazid bin Sinan told me, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told me, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada 26, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: “So he revealed to his servant what he revealed, and he said: His servant Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11021","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “Do you wonder that the appearance is for Abraham, the speech is for Moses, and the vision is for Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11022","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Zirr bin Hubaysh, on the authority of Abdullah, in his saying: And he saw another revelation, in addition to his saying, “He has seen one of the great signs of his Lord.” He said: He saw Gabriel, peace be upon him, blocking the horizon. He only saw him. \"In these two places\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11023","Muhammad bin Hatim told us, he said: Hibban told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Ibn Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, in his saying: “And he saw another incident. He said: The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw Gabriel on the A vast expanse filled what is between the sky and the earth, but he did not see his Lord, Blessed and Most High.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11024","Yahya bin Hakim told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr bin Hubaysh, on the authority of Abdullah On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: And he saw it another time, and he said: “I saw Gabriel, peace be upon him, at the Sidra tree, and he had six hundred wings. From it are scattered the charms of pearls.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11025","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Sufyan told us. H And Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdul God, in His saying: “He has certainly seen of the greatest signs of his Lord.” He said: “He has seen a surge” in the hadith of Abd al-Rahman Akhdar that has blocked the horizon."
"11026","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas He said: I have not seen anything more resembling the word than what Abu Hurairah said, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Indeed, God, Blessed and Most High, has written on The son of Adam has had his share of fornication. He inevitably realized that. Fornication of the hands means oppression, fornication of the tongue means speaking, and the soul means wishing and desiring. And relief: it confirms that or disbelieves it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11027","Ahmad bin Bakkar and Abd al-Hamid bin Muhammad told us, saying: Mukhlid told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of his father, he said: He told me Musaab bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas, on the authority of his father, he said: I swore by Al-Lat and Al-Uzza, and my companions said to me: What you said was miserable, you said in abandonment, So I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I mentioned that to him, and he said: “Say: There is no god but God. He alone has no partner. To Him belongs the dominion and to Him is Praise, and He has power over all things, and blow on your left three times, and seek refuge in God from the accursed Satan, and then do not repeat.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11028","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Miskin bin Bukayr told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, he said: Al-Zuhri told me, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever among you swears an oath and says in his oath: By Al-Lat and Al-Uzza, Let him say: There is no god but Allah.”"
"11029","Ali bin Al-Mundhir told us, he said: Ibn Fudayl told us, he said: Al-Walid bin Juma’ told us, on the authority of Abu Tufayl, he said: When he opened The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Mecca, sent Khalid ibn al-Walid to Nakhlah, which contained an Uzza, so Khaled came to it, and it was on Three stones, so he cut off the stones and demolished the house that was on them. Then he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and informed him, and said: “Go back, for you You did not do anything.” Khalid returned, and when the forest saw him while they were blocking it, they looked at the mountain, saying: Oh Uzza, oh Uzza. Then Khaled came to her and saw that she was a naked woman, with her hair spread, and dust covered on her head. So he cut her with the sword until he killed her. Then he returned to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and told him, and he said: “That is the Uzza.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11030","Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed bin Kathir told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, he said: I asked Aisha, on the authority of the words of God Almighty: “There is no blame on him for circumambulating them. By God, there is no blame on anyone if he does not circumambulate Al-Safa.” And Al-Marwah. Aisha said: What you said is miserable, O my nephew. If this verse were as you interpreted it, there would be no blame on him except Circumambulating them around, but it was revealed that the Ansar, before they submitted to Islam, were preparing for the death of the tyrant, which they used to worship when he was paralyzed. Those who qualified for it used to feel embarrassed to circumambulate Safa and Marwah. When they asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about that, God Almighty revealed: Indeed, Safa and Marwah are among the symbols of God, so whoever makes Hajj to the House or performs Umrah, there is no sin on him if he circumambulates them, then he may The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, enacted circumambulation with them, so no one is permitted to abandon circumambulation with them.”"
"11031","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, meaning Ibn Al-Harith, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad On the authority of Abdullah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “read the stars and prostrated by them.”"
"11032","Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Damra bin Saeed, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, that Omar asked Abu Waqid Al-Laythi: What was the recitation of the Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, during Eid al-Adha and Eid al-Fitr? He said: “He was reciting the Qur’an and the Glorious Qur’an, and the Hour approached and the moon split open.”"
"11033","Ahmad bin Saeed told us, he said: Yunus told us, he said: Falayh told us, on the authority of Damrah bin Saeed, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, On the authority of Abu Waqid Al-Laythi, he said: Omar asked me about what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited in the Eid prayer, and I said: “The Hour has approached.” And the moon split open, and the Glorious Qur’an."
"11034","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala informed us, on the authority of Khaled, who is Ibn al-Harith, who said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Sulayman, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Muammar, on the authority of Abdullah, said: The moon was split into two parts at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, one part above the mountain, and one part The mountain will cover it, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O God, bear witness.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11035","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Muammar, on the authority of Abdullah, He said: During the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the moon was split into two parts, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Bear witness.”"
"11036","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala informed us, on the authority of Muhammad, who was Ibn Thawr, on the authority of Muammar. H And Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, he said: He asked The people of Mecca gave the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, a sign, and the moon split twice in Mecca, and if they saw a sign they would turn away and say, “Continuous magic.” He says: Going (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11037","Amr bin Ali told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, he said: Shu`bah told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told me, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abd God, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited: “Is there anyone who will remember?”"
"11038","Abu Salih told us, he said: Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Masoud bin Malik, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I was victorious with youth, and Aad was destroyed with the hornet.”"
"11039","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Wahhab told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said while he was at the dome of Badr on the day of Badr: “O God, I adjure you to make your covenant and your promise. O God, if you wish, you will not be worshiped.” After this day,” Abu Bakr took him by the hand and said: “It is sufficient for you, O Messenger of God, for you insisted on your Lord while He was in the armor. So he went out and said: The crowd will be defeated and turn back. {45} Rather, the Hour is their appointed time, and the Hour is worse and more bitter {46}.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11040","Yusuf bin Saeed told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Yusuf bin Mahak told me, he said: I am with Aisha’s mother. The believers, when an Iraqi came to her and said: O Mother of the Believers, show me your Qur’an. She said: Why? He said: I want to compose the Qur’an for him, for we recite it with us without a compilation. She said: Woe to you, and what harm you, which one have you read before? ! The first Surah of Al-Mufassal was revealed, in which there was mention of Paradise and Hell, so that when the people converted to Islam, the lawful and the forbidden were revealed, even if The first thing that was revealed was: Do not drink alcohol. They said: We do not stop drinking alcohol. And if the first thing was revealed: Do not commit adultery, they would have said: We do not stop adultery. And it was revealed: And the hour is more terrible, and I am passing through Mecca, and I am a slave girl playing with Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Surah Al-Baqarah was not revealed except while I was “He is with him,” he said: “Then he brought out the Qur’an to him, and I recited the surahs over him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11041","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: Yunus bin Yusuf told me, on the authority of Suleiman bin To the left, he said: The people dispersed to meet Abu Hurairah, and Natil said to him: O Sheikh, tell me a hadith that you heard. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “The first people to be judged on the Day of Resurrection will be three people: a man who was martyred, and he was brought to him and he made known his blessings, and he recognized them. He said: What Did you work there? He said: I fought for you until I was martyred. He said: You lied, but you fought because it would be said: So-and-so is bold. It was said, then he was ordered to be withdrawn. On his face, until he was thrown into the Fire, and a man learned knowledge and taught it, and read the Qur’an, and it was brought to him, and he made known to him his blessings, and he recognized them. He said: What Did you work there? He said: I learned knowledge and taught it, and I recited the Qur’an in you. He said: You lied, but you learned knowledge so that it can be said: a scholar, and you recited the Qur’an. To be said: A reader, so it was said, then he was ordered to be dragged on his face until he was thrown into the Fire, and there was a man whom God expanded upon and gave him various kinds of blessings. All the money. Then it was brought to him and he showed him his blessings and he recognized them. He said: What did you do with it? He said: I did not leave any way in which you would like to be spent without spending. In it is yours. He said: You lied, but you did it so that it would be said: Jawad. It was said, then he was ordered to be dragged on his face until he was thrown into the Fire. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11042","Ali bin Hajar told us, Ismail told us, he said: Muhammad bin Abi Harmala told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, on the authority of Abu Darda’, He heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, as he was being narrated on the pulpit, saying: “And for whoever fears the standing before his Lord, there are two gardens.” So I said: And if he commits adultery And if he steals, O Messenger of God? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said the second time: And for whoever fears standing before his Lord there are two gardens. So I said the second time: And if he He committed adultery, and if he stole, O Messenger of God? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said in the third time: And for whoever fears standing before his Lord, there are two gardens. I said: Third: Even if he commits adultery, and if he steals, O Messenger of God, he said: Even if it pleases Abu Darda’. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11043","Mu'mal bin Hisham told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, he said: Musa told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas, Abu Al-Darda’ said: On the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he recited it: “And for whoever fears standing before his Lord there are two gardens,” so I said: And if He committed adultery, even if he committed theft, O Messenger of God. He said: And for anyone who fears the position of his Lord, there are two gardens. He said: I said: Even if he committed adultery, or if he committed theft, O Messenger of God? And for whoever fears standing before his Lord there will be two gardens, even if he commits adultery, even if he steals, despite Abu Darda’’s displeasure.” I continued to recite it like that until he met him and prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11044","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abu Abd al-Samad told us, he said: Abu Imran al-Juni told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdullah Ibn Qays, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, in Paradise there is a tent made of a hollow pearl.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11045","Abu Ali Muhammad bin Yahya told us, he said: Abdullah bin Uthman told us, he said: Abdullah bin Yahya told us, he said: Yahya bin Hassan, on the authority of Rabia bin Amer, said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Advance yourself to the One who has majesty and honor.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11046","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Indeed, in Paradise there is a tree in the shade of which a rider can travel for a hundred years.”"
"11047","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Abu Awanah, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “The Qur’an was sent down in its entirety on the Night of Decree to the lowest heaven, then it was separated and revealed over the years. That is his saying: I swear by the positions of the stars.”"
"11048","Bishr bin Hilal told us, he said: Ja’far, meaning Ibn Sulayman, told us, on the authority of one-eyed Harun, on the authority of Badil, who is Ibn Maysara, on the authority of Abd. Allah Ibn Shaqiq, on the authority of Aisha, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite: Joy, basil, and a garden of bliss.”"
"11049","Al-Hussein bin Harith informed us, he said: Al-Fadl bin Musa informed us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Sa’id, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “There were kings after Jesus, peace be upon him, who changed the Torah and the Gospel, and among them were believers who recited The Torah and the Gospel, so it was said to their kings: We do not find a curse worse than the curse of those who curse us. They read: And who does not judge? In what God has sent down, those are the disbelievers. These are the verses, along with what they fault us with of our deeds in reciting them, so call upon them and let them recite as they We read, and let them believe as we believed. So he called them and gathered them together and proposed that they be killed or they should abandon reading the Torah and the Gospel, unless they changed it. They said: Whatever you want, invite us, and a group of them said: Build us a cylinder, then raise us to it, then give us Something with which to raise our food and drink, so we will not respond to you, and a group said: Let us wander through the land, and wander and drink as a wild animal drinks. If you gain power over us in your land, then kill us, and a group says: Build us a house in the desert, and we will dig wells and cultivate crops, but we will not be rejected. And monasticism. They invented it. We did not prescribe it for them except to seek the pleasure of God, but they did not observe it as it was properly cared for. And the others said: We worship as so-and-so worshiped. And we will move as so-and-so did, and we will take a turn as so-and-so took, and they are in their polytheism, having no knowledge of the faith of those they follow. So when he was sent The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and only a few of them remained. A man descended from his cell, and a tourist came from his tour, and the owner of the monastery from... His monastery, so they believed in him and believed in him, so God Almighty said: O you who have believed, fear God and believe in His Messenger. He will give you two pledges of His mercy, they were rewarded by their belief in Jesus, son of Mary, and their belief in the Torah and the Gospel, and their belief in Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: And He gives you a light by which you may walk, the Qur’an and their following of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: So that the people of The Book: Those who imitate you are not capable of anything of the bounty of God, and that bounty is in the hand of God. He gives it to whom He wills, and God is of \"The great virtue\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11050","Harun bin Saeed told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Amr bin Al-Harith told me, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Hilal, on the authority of Aoun bin Abdullah bin Utba, on the authority of his father, that Ibn Masoud said: “There was nothing between our conversion to Islam and God blaming us for this.” Verse: Has not the time come for those who have believed that their hearts should submit to the remembrance of God except four years?"
"11051","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Al-Ala, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “When the people of Paradise enter Paradise, and the people of Hell enter Hell, death will be brought, clad in the veil, and it will stand on the wall that separates the people of Hell.” Paradise and the people of Hell, then he will be slaughtered on the wall, then it will be said: O people of Paradise, eternity not death, and O people of Hell, eternity not death.”"
"11052","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Jarir informed us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Tamim bin Salamah, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that She said: “Praise be to God, whose hearing encompasses voices. A female servant came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, complaining about her husband. Her words are hidden from me, so God Almighty revealed: God has heard the words of the woman who disputes with you about her husband and complains to God, and God hears. Communicate with you, the verse."
"11053","Yusuf bin Issa informed us, he said: Al-Fadl bin Musa informed us, he said: Al-Amash informed us, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, She said: A Jew entered the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Peace be upon you. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “And upon you.” Aisha said: May the poison and wrath of God be upon you. He said: Then the Jew came out, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O Aisha, God, Blessed and Most High, does not love “The indecent and obscene one.” She said: O Messenger of God, do you not know what he said? He said: “And what did he say?” She said: He said: May God bless you, which is what he said: And when they come to you, they greet you with a way that God has not greeted you with. He said: Then he left. The Jew was saying to himself and himself, so God Almighty revealed: And they say within themselves: Why would God not punish us for what we say? Hell is sufficient for them, which they will visit, so wretched is the destination.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11054","Saeed bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that a group of Jews They entered upon the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and said: May peace be upon you. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “On you.” Aisha said: So I said: Rather, upon you. Poison and curse. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O Aisha, “God loves gentleness in all matters.” Aisha said: So I said: O Messenger of God, do you hear what they said? He said: “I said: On you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11055","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “burned a palm tree.” Bani An-Nadir and he cut off, which is Al-Buwayrah, so God, Blessed and Most High, revealed: What of the linah you cut down or leave standing on its roots. So, by God’s permission, may He disgrace the transgressors.”"
